IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa1-part4-capacity`

-- coa1-tests-part4.l4: tests for coa1-part4-capacity.l4 (ss 39 to 52 of the Companies Act 2006).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section's words (quoted beside each group) before the run, and is written beside
-- the assertion; none was copied from the module's own output. Arguments follow the GIVEN order of each rule. Dates and pound amounts
-- are illustrative test inputs, not figures from the Act. A DEONTIC value cannot be compared in an #ASSERT on the stable binary, so
-- each #TRACE states its expected outcome in a comment and is read, not asserted.

-- ---- s 39 ----
-- "(1) The validity of an act done by a company shall not be called into question on the ground of lack of capacity by reason of anything in the company's constitution. (2) This section has effect subject to section 42"
#ASSERT `s 39(1) the validity of the act can be called into question on the ground of lack of capacity` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39(1) the validity of the act can be called into question on the ground of lack of capacity` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39(1) the validity of the act can be called into question on the ground of lack of capacity` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 39(1) the validity of the act can be called into question on the ground of lack of capacity` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 40 ----
-- "(2) For this purpose— (a) a person “deals with” a company if he is a party to any transaction or other act to which the company is a party"
#ASSERT `s 40(2)(a) the person deals with the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(2)(a) the person deals with the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(b) a person dealing with a company— (i) is not bound to enquire as to any limitation ..., (ii) is presumed to have acted in good faith unless the contrary is proved, and (iii) is not to be regarded as acting in bad faith by reason only of his knowing that an act is beyond the powers of the directors"
#ASSERT `s 40(2)(b)(i) the person dealing with the company is bound to enquire as to any limitation on the powers of the directors` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40(2)(b)(i) the person dealing with the company is bound to enquire as to any limitation on the powers of the directors` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 40(2)(b)(ii) the person dealing with the company is presumed to have acted in good faith` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(2)(b)(ii) the person dealing with the company is presumed to have acted in good faith` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40(2)(b)(ii) the person dealing with the company is presumed to have acted in good faith` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 40(2)(b)(iii) the person is regarded as acting in bad faith by reason only of knowing that an act is beyond the powers of the directors` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40(2)(b)(iii) the person is regarded as acting in bad faith by reason only of knowing that an act is beyond the powers of the directors` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 40(2)(b)(iii) the person is regarded as acting in bad faith by reason only of knowing that an act is beyond the powers of the directors` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(1) In favour of a person dealing with a company in good faith, the power of the directors to bind the company, or authorise others to do so, is deemed to be free of any limitation under the company's constitution."
#ASSERT `s 40(1) the power of the directors to bind the company is deemed free of any limitation under the company's constitution in favour of the person` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(1) the power of the directors to bind the company is deemed free of any limitation under the company's constitution in favour of the person` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(1) the power of the directors to bind the company is deemed free of any limitation under the company's constitution in favour of the person` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 40(1) the power of the directors to bind the company is deemed free of any limitation under the company's constitution in favour of the person` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 40(1) the power of the directors to bind the company is deemed free of any limitation under the company's constitution in favour of the person` FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(3) The references above to limitations on the directors' powers under the company's constitution include limitations deriving— (a) from a resolution ..., or (b) from any agreement between the members"
#ASSERT `s 40(3) the limitation is a limitation under the company's constitution for the purposes of section 40` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(3) the limitation is a limitation under the company's constitution for the purposes of section 40` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(3) the limitation is a limitation under the company's constitution for the purposes of section 40` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(4) This section does not affect any right of a member of the company to bring proceedings to restrain the doing of an action that is beyond the powers of the directors. But no such proceedings lie in respect of an act to be done in fulfilment of a legal obligation arising from a previous act of the company."
#ASSERT `s 40(4) this section affects any right of a member to bring proceedings to restrain the doing of an action that is beyond the powers of the directors` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40(4) proceedings lie to restrain the act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 40(4) proceedings lie to restrain the act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(5) This section does not affect any liability incurred by the directors, or any other person, by reason of the directors' exceeding their powers."
#ASSERT `s 40(5) this section affects any liability incurred by the directors or any other person by reason of the directors' exceeding their powers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(6) This section has effect subject to— section 41 (transactions with directors or their associates), and section 42 (companies that are charities)."
#ASSERT `s 40(6) this section has effect subject to section 41 or section 42` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(6) this section has effect subject to section 41 or section 42` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40(6) this section has effect subject to section 41 or section 42` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 40(6) this section has effect subject to section 41 or section 42` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 41 ----
-- "(1) This section applies to a transaction if or to the extent that its validity depends on section 40 ... Nothing in this section shall be read as excluding the operation of any other enactment or rule of law"
#ASSERT `s 41(1) this section applies to the transaction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(1) this section applies to the transaction` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(1) this section excludes the operation of any other enactment or rule of law by virtue of which the transaction may be called in question or any liability to the company may arise` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(2) Where— (a) a company enters into such a transaction, and (b) the parties to the transaction include— (i) a director of the company or of its holding company, or (ii) a person connected with any such director, the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company."
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the transaction is voidable at the instance of the company` TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(3) Whether or not it is avoided, any such party ... and any director of the company who authorised the transaction, is liable— (a) to account to the company for any gain he has made directly or indirectly by the transaction, and (b) to indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction."
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the person is liable under subsection (3)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the person is liable under subsection (3)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the person is liable under subsection (3)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3)(a) the amount the person must account to the company for` (JUST TRUE) 500 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 41(3)(a) the amount the person must account to the company for` (JUST FALSE) 500 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 41(3)(a) the amount the person must account to the company for` NOTHING 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3)(b) the amount the person must indemnify the company for` (JUST TRUE) 300 EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 41(3)(b) the amount the person must indemnify the company for` (JUST FALSE) 300 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 41(3)(b) the amount the person must indemnify the company for` NOTHING 300 EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(4) The transaction ceases to be voidable if— (a) restitution ... is no longer possible, or (b) the company is indemnified ..., or (c) rights acquired bona fide for value and without actual notice ... would be affected by the avoidance, or (d) the transaction is affirmed by the company."
#ASSERT `s 41(4) the transaction has ceased to be voidable` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(4) the transaction has ceased to be voidable` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(4) the transaction has ceased to be voidable` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(4) the transaction has ceased to be voidable` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(4) the transaction has ceased to be voidable` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(5) A person other than a director of the company is not liable under subsection (3) if he shows that at the time the transaction was entered into he did not know that the directors were exceeding their powers."
#ASSERT `s 41(5) a person other than a director is liable under subsection (3)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(5) a person other than a director is liable under subsection (3)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(5) a person other than a director is liable under subsection (3)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(6) Nothing in the preceding provisions of this section affects the rights of any party to the transaction not within subsection (2)(b)(i) or (ii). But the court may, on the application of the company or any such party, make an order affirming, severing or setting aside the transaction"
#ASSERT `s 41(6) the preceding provisions of section 41 affect the rights of the party` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(6) the preceding provisions of section 41 affect the rights of the party` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(6) the court may make an order affirming, severing or setting aside the transaction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(6) the court may make an order affirming, severing or setting aside the transaction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(7) In this section— (a) “transaction” includes any act; and (b) the reference to a person connected with a director has the same meaning as in Part 10 (company directors)."
#ASSERT `s 41(7)(a) the thing is a transaction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(7)(a) the thing is a transaction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(7)(b) the person is a person connected with a director` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(7)(b) the person is a person connected with a director` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(7)(b) the person is a person connected with a director` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 42 ----
-- "(5) This section does not extend to Scotland (but see section 112 of the Companies Act 1989 (c. 40))."
#ASSERT `s 42(5) this section extends to the company` `Scotland` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(5) this section extends to the company` `England and Wales` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(5) this section extends to the company` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(1) Sections 39 and 40 ... do not apply to the acts of a company that is a charity except in favour of a person who— (a) does not know at the time the act is done that the company is a charity, or (b) gives full consideration in money or money's worth in relation to the act and does not know (as the case may be)— (i) that the act is not permitted by the company's constitution, or (ii) that the act is beyond the powers of the directors."
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 39 does not apply to the act` `Scotland` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 39 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 39 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 39 does not apply to the act` `Northern Ireland` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 39 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 39 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 39 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 39 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 40 does not apply to the act` `Scotland` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 40 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 40 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 40 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 40 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 40 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42(1) section 40 does not apply to the act` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "(2) Where a company that is a charity purports to transfer or grant an interest in property, the fact that ... does not affect the title of a person who subsequently acquires the property or any interest in it for full consideration without actual notice of any such circumstances"
#ASSERT `s 42(2) the title of the person who acquires the property or interest is affected` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(2) the title of the person who acquires the property or interest is affected` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(2) the title of the person who acquires the property or interest is affected` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(2) the title of the person who acquires the property or interest is affected` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(2) the title of the person who acquires the property or interest is affected` `England and Wales` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(2) the title of the person who acquires the property or interest is affected` `Scotland` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(3) In any proceedings arising out of subsection (1) or (2) the burden of proving— (a) that a person knew that the company was a charity, or (b) ... lies on the person asserting that fact."
#ASSERT `s 42(3) the burden of proving the fact lies on the person` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42(3) the burden of proving the fact lies on the person` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(3) the burden of proving the fact lies on the person` `England and Wales` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(3) the burden of proving the fact lies on the person` `Scotland` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(4) In the case of a company that is a charity the affirmation of a transaction to which section 41 applies ... is ineffective without the prior written consent of— (a) in England and Wales, the Charity Commission; (b) in Northern Ireland, the Department for Social Development."
#ASSERT `s 42(4) the affirmation of the transaction is effective` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(4) the affirmation of the transaction is effective` `Northern Ireland` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 42(4) the affirmation of the transaction is effective` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(4) the affirmation of the transaction is effective` `England and Wales` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(4) the affirmation of the transaction is effective` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42(4) the affirmation of the transaction is effective` `Scotland` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 43 ----
-- "(1) Under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland a contract may be made— (a) by a company, by writing under its common seal, or (b) on behalf of a company, by a person acting under its authority, express or implied."
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the contract may be made in that way` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the contract may be made in that way` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the contract may be made in that way` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 43(1) the contract may be made in that way` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(2) Any formalities required by law in the case of a contract made by an individual also apply, unless a contrary intention appears, to a contract made by or on behalf of a company."
#ASSERT `s 43(2) the formalities required of an individual apply to the contract` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 43(2) the formalities required of an individual apply to the contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 43(2) the formalities required of an individual apply to the contract` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 43(2) the formalities required of an individual apply to the contract` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 44 ----
-- "(1) Under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland a document is executed by a company— (a) by the affixing of its common seal, or (b) by signature in accordance with the following provisions."
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the document is executed by the company` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the document is executed by the company` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the document is executed by the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(1) the document is executed by the company` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(2) A document is validly executed by a company if it is signed on behalf of the company— (a) by two authorised signatories, or (b) by a director of the company in the presence of a witness who attests the signature."
#ASSERT `s 44(2) signature in that way validly executes the document for the company` 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(2) signature in that way validly executes the document for the company` 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(2) signature in that way validly executes the document for the company` 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(2) signature in that way validly executes the document for the company` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(2) signature in that way validly executes the document for the company` 1 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "(3) The following are “authorised signatories” for the purposes of subsection (2)— (a) every director of the company, and (b) in the case of a private company with a secretary or a public company, the secretary (or any joint secretary) of the company."
#ASSERT `s 44(3) the person is an authorised signatory for the purposes of subsection (2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(3) the person is an authorised signatory for the purposes of subsection (2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(3) the person is an authorised signatory for the purposes of subsection (2)` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(3) the person is an authorised signatory for the purposes of subsection (2)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(3) the person is an authorised signatory for the purposes of subsection (2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(4) A document signed in accordance with subsection (2) and expressed, in whatever words, to be executed by the company has the same effect as if executed under the common seal of the company."
#ASSERT `s 44(4) the document has the same effect as if executed under the common seal of the company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(4) the document has the same effect as if executed under the common seal of the company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(4) the document has the same effect as if executed under the common seal of the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(5) In favour of a purchaser a document is deemed to have been duly executed by a company if it purports to be signed in accordance with subsection (2). A “purchaser” means a purchaser in good faith for valuable consideration and includes a lessee, mortgagee or other person who for valuable consideration acquires an interest in property."
#ASSERT `s 44(5) the person is a purchaser` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(5) the person is a purchaser` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(5) the person is a purchaser` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(5) the document is deemed to have been duly executed by the company in favour of the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(5) the document is deemed to have been duly executed by the company in favour of the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(5) the document is deemed to have been duly executed by the company in favour of the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(6) Where a document is to be signed by a person on behalf of more than one company, it is not duly signed by that person for the purposes of this section unless he signs it separately in each capacity."
#ASSERT `s 44(6) the document is duly signed by the person for the purposes of section 44` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(6) the document is duly signed by the person for the purposes of section 44` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 44(6) the document is duly signed by the person for the purposes of section 44` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(7) References in this section to a document being (or purporting to be) signed by a director or secretary are to be read, in a case where that office is held by a firm, as references to its being (or purporting to be) signed by an individual authorised by the firm to sign on its behalf."
#ASSERT `s 44(7) the document is read as signed by the director or secretary` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(7) the document is read as signed by the director or secretary` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 44(7) the document is read as signed by the director or secretary` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(8) This section applies to a document that is (or purports to be) executed by a company in the name of or on behalf of another person whether or not that person is also a company."
#ASSERT `s 44(8) this section applies to the document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 44(8) this section applies to the document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 45 ----
-- "(6) This section does not form part of the law of Scotland."
#ASSERT `s 45(6) this section forms part of the law that applies to the company` `Scotland` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45(6) this section forms part of the law that applies to the company` `England and Wales` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(1) A company may have a common seal, but need not have one."
#ASSERT `s 45(1) the company may have a common seal` `England and Wales` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 45(1) the company may have a common seal` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 45(1) the company may have a common seal` `Scotland` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 45(1) the company need have a common seal` `England and Wales` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45(1) the company need have a common seal` `Scotland` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(2) A company which has a common seal shall have its name engraved in legible characters on the seal."
#ASSERT `s 45(2) the company must have its name engraved in legible characters on its common seal` `England and Wales` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 45(2) the company must have its name engraved in legible characters on its common seal` `England and Wales` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45(2) the company must have its name engraved in legible characters on its common seal` `Scotland` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the duty, run (read, not asserted). Expected, in order: FULFILLED (name engraved); the standing obligation (the seal has no name engraved yet, no time limit in the text); FULFILLED (no common seal, nothing is owed).
#TRACE `s 45(2) the company's duty to engrave its name on its common seal` `England and Wales` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 45(2) engrave the company's name in legible characters on the common seal` AT 3
#TRACE `s 45(2) the company's duty to engrave its name on its common seal` `England and Wales` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
#TRACE `s 45(2) the company's duty to engrave its name on its common seal` `England and Wales` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
-- "(3) If a company fails to comply with subsection (2) an offence is committed by— (a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default."
#ASSERT `s 45(3)(a) the company commits an offence` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 45(3)(a) the company commits an offence` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45(3)(a) the company commits an offence` `England and Wales` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45(3)(a) the company commits an offence` `Scotland` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 45(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 45(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 45(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 45(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` `Scotland` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(4) An officer of a company, or a person acting on behalf of a company, commits an offence if he uses, or authorises the use of, a seal purporting to be a seal of the company on which its name is not engraved as required by subsection (2)."
#ASSERT `s 45(4) the person commits an offence` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 45(4) the person commits an offence` `England and Wales` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45(4) the person commits an offence` `England and Wales` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45(4) the person commits an offence` `England and Wales` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45(4) the person commits an offence` `Scotland` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the prohibition, run (read, not asserted). Expected, in order: BREACH (the use is the forbidden act); the prohibition still standing (the text gives no time limit, so no deadline passes and it is never discharged by waiting).
#TRACE `s 45(4) the prohibition` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 45(4) an officer of a company, or a person acting on behalf of a company` DOES `s 45(4) use, or authorise the use of, a seal purporting to be a seal of the company on which its name is not engraved` AT 2
#TRACE `s 45(4) the prohibition` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
-- "(5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale." (no daily default fine)
#ASSERT `s 45(5) the penalty`'s `how convicted` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 45(5) the penalty`'s `fine not exceeding` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 45(5) the penalty`'s `daily default fine for continued contravention` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 45(5) the penalty`'s `imprisonment not exceeding` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 45(5) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS 1000

-- ---- s 46 ----
-- "(1) A document is validly executed by a company as a deed ... if, and only if— (a) it is duly executed by the company, and (b) it is delivered as a deed."
#ASSERT `s 46(1) the document is validly executed by the company as a deed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46(1) the document is validly executed by the company as a deed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46(1) the document is validly executed by the company as a deed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b) a document is presumed to be delivered upon its being executed, unless a contrary intention is proved."
#ASSERT `s 46(2) the document is presumed to be delivered` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46(2) the document is presumed to be delivered` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46(2) the document is presumed to be delivered` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 47 ----
-- "(1) Under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland a company may, by instrument executed as a deed, empower a person ... as its attorney to execute deeds or other documents on its behalf. (2) A deed or other document so executed, whether in the United Kingdom or elsewhere, has effect as if executed by the company."
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the company may empower the person as its attorney to execute deeds or other documents on its behalf` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the company may empower the person as its attorney to execute deeds or other documents on its behalf` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the company may empower the person as its attorney to execute deeds or other documents on its behalf` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the deed or other document has effect as if executed by the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the deed or other document has effect as if executed by the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 48 ----
-- "(2) Notwithstanding the provisions of any enactment, a company need not have a company seal. (3) ... a document signed or subscribed (or, in the case of an electronic document, authenticated) by or on behalf of the company in accordance with the provisions of the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995 has effect as if so executed."
#ASSERT `s 48(2) the company need have a company seal` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(2) the company need have a company seal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the document has effect as if executed by the affixing of the common seal` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the document has effect as if executed by the affixing of the common seal` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the document has effect as if executed by the affixing of the common seal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the document has effect as if executed by the affixing of the common seal` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the document has effect as if executed by the affixing of the common seal` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 49 ----
-- "(1) A company that has a common seal may have an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom."
#ASSERT `s 49(1) the company may have an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(1) the company may have an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 49(1) the company may have an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a grant ("may have") limited by the relative clause "that has a common seal", not closed with "only", so a company without a common seal is outside the limit and the text is silent (Guide, section 5, "In short"), fork F43
-- "(2) The official seal must be a facsimile of the company's common seal, with the addition on its face of the place or places where it is to be used."
#ASSERT `s 49(2) the official seal meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(2) the official seal meets the requirements` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 49(2) the official seal meets the requirements` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(3) The official seal when duly affixed to a document has the same effect as the company's common seal. This subsection does not extend to Scotland."
#ASSERT `s 49(3) the official seal has the same effect as the company's common seal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(3) the official seal has the same effect as the company's common seal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 49(3) the official seal has the same effect as the company's common seal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(4) A company having an official seal for use outside the United Kingdom may— (a) by writing under its common seal, or (b) as respects Scotland, by writing subscribed or authenticated in accordance with the Requirements of Writing (Scotland) Act 1995, authorise any person appointed for the purpose to affix the official seal"
#ASSERT `s 49(4) the company may authorise the person to affix the official seal` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(4) the company may authorise the person to affix the official seal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(4) the company may authorise the person to affix the official seal` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 49(4) the company may authorise the person to affix the official seal` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 49(4) the company may authorise the person to affix the official seal` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(5) As between the company and a person dealing with such an agent, the agent's authority continues— (a) during the period mentioned in the instrument conferring the authority, or (b) if no period is mentioned, until notice of the revocation or termination of the agent's authority has been given to the person dealing with him."
#ASSERT `s 49(5) the agent's authority continues on the date` FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 49(5) the agent's authority continues on the date` TRUE (JUST (Date 31 12 2026)) NOTHING (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(5) the agent's authority continues on the date` TRUE (JUST (Date 31 12 2026)) NOTHING (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 49(5) the agent's authority continues on the date` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(5) the agent's authority continues on the date` TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 10 6 2026)) (Date 9 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(5) the agent's authority continues on the date` TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 10 6 2026)) (Date 10 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 49(5) the agent's authority continues on the date` TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 10 6 2026)) (Date 11 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 49(5) the agent's authority continues on the date` TRUE (JUST (Date 31 12 2026)) (JUST (Date 1 3 2026)) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "(6) The person affixing the official seal must certify in writing on the deed or other document to which the seal is affixed the date on which, and place at which, it is affixed."
#ASSERT `s 49(6) the person affixing the official seal has certified the date and place` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(6) the person affixing the official seal has certified the date and place` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 49(6) the person affixing the official seal has certified the date and place` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the duty, run (read, not asserted). Expected, in order: FULFILLED; the standing obligation (nothing certified, no time limit in the text).
#TRACE `s 49(6) the duty of the person affixing the official seal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 49(6) the person affixing the official seal` DOES `s 49(6) certify in writing on the deed or other document the date on which, and place at which, the official seal is affixed` AT 1
#TRACE `s 49(6) the duty of the person affixing the official seal` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- ---- s 50 ----
-- "(1) A company that has a common seal may have an official seal for use— (a) for sealing securities issued by the company, or (b) for sealing documents creating or evidencing securities so issued."
#ASSERT `s 50(1) the company may have an official seal for the use` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 50(1) the company may have an official seal for the use` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a grant ("may have") limited by the relative clause "that has a common seal", not closed with "only", so a company without a common seal is outside the limit and the text is silent (Guide, section 5, "In short"), fork F44
#ASSERT `s 50(1) the company may have an official seal for the use` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 50(1) the company may have an official seal for the use` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 50(1) the company may have an official seal for the use` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(2) The official seal— (a) must be a facsimile of the common seal, with the addition on its face of the word “Securities”, and (b) when duly affixed to the document has the same effect as the company's common seal."
#ASSERT `s 50(2)(a) the official seal meets the requirements` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 50(2)(a) the official seal meets the requirements` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 50(2)(a) the official seal meets the requirements` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 50(2)(b) the official seal has the same effect as the company's common seal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 50(2)(b) the official seal has the same effect as the company's common seal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 51 and s 52 ----
-- "(1) A contract that purports to be made by or on behalf of a company at a time when the company has not been formed has effect, subject to any agreement to the contrary, as one made with the person purporting to act for the company or as agent for it, and he is personally liable on the contract accordingly."
#ASSERT `s 51(1) the person purporting to act for the company is personally liable on the contract` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
